l 3 at once.\n\n**Better strategy**: Play a lower card (♣J or ♣Q) to force the Landlord to use their last card NOW, then my teammate or I can beat it.\n\nReason:\nI should play ♣Q. This puts significant pressure on the Landlord with only 1 card remaining. If the Landlord has a card higher than Q (K, A, 2, or Jokers), they\'ll likely be forced to play it. Then my teammate (with 3 cards) or I (with BlackJoker, K, J remaining) can potentially beat it. If the Landlord passes, I maintain control and can continue applying pressure. Playing Q is better than J because it reduces the Landlord\'s options while keeping my BlackJoker and K as insurance.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣Q"]}'}
